  {
   "text": "The box and lid are built, but the part does not pass the plan check yet, so I have not moved on to slicing or printing.\n\n- **Passes:** overall size is 60.02 x 40 x 30 mm, and the body is closed.\n- **Fails, minimum wall:** the box knuckles are centred 2 mm from the back face, so they touch it and leave a 0.01 mm sliver. That is the real defect.\n- **Fails, hinge pin:** the check looks for a hole, but I built a 2 mm pin, so the plan's wording does not match the part.\n- **Fails, feature count:** I used 10 steps against the planned 5, so this is a plan mismatch rather than a geometry problem.\n\nThe clearance is 0.4 mm around the knuckles and the pin has 0.2 mm radial clearance in the lid bore. The lid is a 9.6 mm cap over the box rim, and the pin is fused to the box knuckles only, so the lid should swing free. I have not checked that the lid actually moves in Model.\n\nDo you want me to move the hinge axis about 2 mm in from the back face so the wall sliver goes away? That means rebuilding the knuckles and lid clearance cuts, and I would re-run the check after."
